//! The axum application: the route groups, their middleware stacks and the listener. Layers apply
//! bottom-up, so the last `route_layer` call runs outermost (WASM before auth before tenant
//! resolution before admission). Admission is chosen once at startup by `AdmissionMode::from_config`:
//! the priority scheduler or the legacy `ConcurrencyLimitLayer`, never both. Handlers take typed
//! bodies by value and hand them to `RouterTrait` methods.
